Friday lunchtime in the centre of  Glasgow this was a chaotic harrowing  scene armed police officers rushed to  the park in inside the hotel they shot a  man dead but not before a number of  people had been stabbed witnesses heard  at least one shot fired and spoke of a  blood strewn scene when I went down  about to take the leaf the leaf inside  the leaf it was covered with blood so I  did not take the leave and I went down  to the stairs when I went down to the  stairs that's where I saw the whole  reception area was covered with blood so  what happened was I saw that one of the  reception got stabbed and he was lying  behind the desk of the reception behind  the reception his desk he was lying and  he was gasping for air witnesses spoke  of stab victims inside and outside the  building paramedics and protective suits  treated casualties on the pavement we  kind of just heard everything looked out  the window and within a few minutes went  downstairs to see what was actually  happening I could see someone lying on a  curb but I wasn't sure whether they'd  been hit with a brick or something like  that and then we saw them on the steps  they were bleeding from the torso  fortunately loss of life police sent the  six people injured included a 42 year  old mill police officer taken to  hospital with stab wounds and in a  critical condition as armed officers  left the scene police Scotland ruled out  terrorism as a factor and issued a  statement on events inside the park in  and those involved officers were on the  scene within two minutes and armed  officers shortly afterwards and the  incident was quickly contained  a man was shot by armed police and have  subsequently died six other men in  hospital for treatment  including a 42 year old police officer  who is in a critical but stable  condition  the Park Inn is one of a number of  hotels in this city used to house asylum  seekers and refugees since the start of  the corona virus pandemic campaigners on  their behalf  have one complained that they have been  living in intolerable conditions which  were having a significant impact on  their mental health this has been a  dreadful afternoon for the city of  Glasgow and particularly for those who  have been directly involved those  injured obviously but there will have  been people who witnessed it this  afternoon particularly in the location  of this incident at quite horrific  events and I think I will not be alone  across Scotland tonight and thinking of  everybody who has in any way been  affected by what unfolded investigations  into what happened here will continue  long after the scene here has cleared  those inquiries are for the longer term  the more immediate concern is coming to  terms with the carnage that unfolded on  this city centre Street
 

